**5 [[Miz Devil]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**2 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
**5 [[Miz Devil]]s spawn after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**1 [[Red Cyclone]] spawns after 96.67 seconds<sup>2,900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
As the gimmick this time around suggests, everything is dirt cheap, so taking advantage of normally high performance but expensive cats like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] plays a huge part in your success against these monstrous stages.

This stage is quite simple: there is barely any sustained pushing power up until Red Cyclone spawns, which means it's very easy to stall with what otherwise would be expensive tanks/CCs like [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]], and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], alongside an ordinary meatshield like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]. As long as you keep chipping down Puffsley's Comet with [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cats]], the initial set of boss enemies simply cannot break through such a healthy defensive wall. Red Cyclone can be dealt with using [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], but stalling him is particularly difficult with the constant frontline assault and piercing attacks making it nigh-impossible to stack up expendable crowd-controllers. Backline [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] can take their place, otherwise time Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] with the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]] to land one or two clean hits, then tear through what remains of his HP thereafter. You should be in the clear as soon as the dust settles, but be wary of Scissoroo ambushing you midway through.

